<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index rose 3 points to 1,275.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index rose 3 points to 1,275.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates rose to 1,275 today from 1,272 on May 8, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1358    12.331	  1357    12.317</p>
<p>   1a   1282  9713.000	  1274  9650.000</p>
<p>   2    1519    21.706	  1521    21.733</p>
<p>   2a   1520 12469.000	  1509 12375.000</p>
<p>   3    1356    12.513	  1361    12.558</p>
<p>   3a   1161  9163.000	  1151  9083.000</p>
